.idea/
.claude/*
.junie/

# ...but DO version the shared Claude skills (on-demand context, part of house style).
# Worktrees, launch.json and settings.local.json stay ignored (machine-local).
!.claude/skills/

# Converter staging output (regenerable from the JSON sources)
**/_generated/

# Local virtualenv (uv/venv both land here; recreate with `uv sync`)
.venv

# Python bytecode caches (regenerable)
__pycache__/
**/__pycache__/
*.py[cod]

# Browser/auth session state — contains live credentials, never commit
**/auth_state.json

# Misplaced-paste junk (PyCharm/BetterVoting drops). These keep getting auto-staged;
# ignore them so they never land in a commit. `scripts/check_repo_hygiene.py` (run by
# the pre-commit hook) still WARNS about them, so a real file pasted with a wrong name
# isn't silently lost — see CLAUDE.md for the img/<bv_id>_*.png and *_bv_export.json rules.
**/Ballot Data*.json
**/img_[0-9]*.png
**/image_[0-9]*.png
**/Screenshot*.png
**/Screen Shot*.png
**/* - Copy*

# Scratch brainstorming file (CLAUDE.md workflow step 1: "Nothing here is permanent...
# delete it when done, never commit them") and the _tabulated mirrors a scratch run
# leaves behind. It was tracked by accident, so whatever scenario happened to be parked
# in it got scanned as if it were a curated case. The generators skip temp/trash/scratch
# names on their own, so this is belt-and-braces: the file stays usable as scratch, it
# just can't be committed.
**/trash_delete.yaml
**/trash_delete*_tabulated.txt

# Generated search outputs from the divergence-finder tools (regenerable)
**/star_irv_hits.csv
**/four_way_hits.csv
**/star_irv_divergence_*.csv
**/star_irv_divergence_*_ballots.txt
**/random_star_divergence_*.csv
**/*_ballots.txt
**/star_irv_log.txt
**/four_way_log.txt

# generated by bv_ballot_sheet.py (printable ballots — not source).
# The root-level /*.html guard exists because one-off output names (a
# committed pets.html once slipped through) don't match the ballot patterns;
# no hand-written HTML lives at the repo root.
ballots.html
*_ballots.html
/*.html
# ...except search-engine site-ownership files, which MUST live at the root
# under the exact name the search engine issued (Google Search Console's
# google<token>.html). Without this exception `git add` silently stages
# nothing and the site never serves the file. mkdocs_hooks.py has the matching
# half — mkdocs-same-dir drops root non-documents from the build.
!/google*.html
ballots.pdf
*_ballots.pdf
*_preview.pdf

# MkDocs website build output (regenerate: uv run --group docs mkdocs build)
/site/
